{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792600783,"nonce":"tAMoarhpD3r6HlI8PvWKOSX11aE=","title":"TypeScript: profile fixed startup overhead on small programs","message":"The selective project-cache/worker change improves the 1,000-function fixture substantially, but exact-source NUC measurements still show fixed overhead on small scripts. Nine randomized process samples per mode, idle i5-1250P, frozen release binaries, LLVM selected, baseline threshold 2,000,000,000 and OSR disabled:\n\n- Tiny cold store: previous 5.079 ms -\u003e candidate 5.748 ms; warm hit 4.740 -\u003e 5.325 ms; uncached control 4.920 -\u003e 5.637 ms.\n- Imported graph cold store: 12.898 -\u003e 12.952 ms; warm hit 5.907 -\u003e 6.714 ms; uncached control 9.321 -\u003e 10.129 ms.\n- Wide control: cold 89.506 -\u003e 17.984 ms; warm 8.299 -\u003e 5.623 ms; uncached 16.683 -\u003e 16.759 ms.\n\nThe import warm gap largely appears in the uncached control too; do not attribute it solely to snapshot decoding or adjust promotion thresholds without a phase profile. An earlier worker-only policy left raw HIR after short processes and regressed warm imports further; the final policy finishes small closed graphs inline and uses the cancellable worker for larger reached graphs. Raw entries record release summaries so unrelated bodies can remain encoded.\n\nProfile runtime/LLVM initialization, frontend and linking/registration separately using identical flags/toolchains and a fixed idle CPU where practical. Compare build/code-layout effects as well as executed work. Preserve interpreter-first execution, complete source checking, cached GEP/release facts and non-blocking worker cancellation. Report process wall time independently of internal execution time. Record allocations if changing ownership or metadata flow; do not add deep AST/HIR copies.\n\nReport: /private/tmp/ts-background-nuc-verified.json and /home/raikage/zyntax-ts-background-nuc-verified.json. Candidate /home/raikage/zyntax-ts-background-zynode-verified SHA256 d54ac83bf673726c787a1e1e07a1301c9bba82e045e4fa9235da7a83c435497d; previous /home/raikage/zyntax-ts-cache-zynode-final SHA256 b53bca21e9cb1241f687756d076b6f1d996c7ee45681328866da15932e3226a4. Rust 1.101.0-nightly c36f14571, LLVM 21.1.8. No compiler jobs were observed before any of the 162 samples, busy \u003c=0.670 core, temperatures \u003c=70C, binary hashes stable. Checks were before samples, not continuous monitoring. Local timings excluded because other Cargo/rustc jobs were active.\n\nFollow-up to 48b697dc20d1db83e3cf17d097527aa61f7a9fb53f291b04e30c6f866512052c; parent 0c26889a7cd2c4060eb94ef93fd808c2857089dbf714735ca52b5d071bdb1564. The separate deferred-first-call issue 35cd150f680dded61c271d4f40e3f3ae1db12c0d877987665cde33a3cb186160 remains relevant to library decoding, but these uncached controls establish a broader fixed-cost investigation.","files":null}]}